\section*{Motivation and formal criterion}

The benchmark questions are conditional: they ask which entities suit a task \emph{when} several further conditions hold at once. A single relevance score answers a different question, topical similarity to the whole sentence, and so rewards an on-topic candidate that fails a stated condition. V2 separates recall of plausible entities from per-condition evidence.

A question is parsed by a deterministic extractive parser into literal spans: a core task, requirements and exclusions. The positive set is the core plus the requirements; exclusions affect tiers only, because similarity to an excluded condition cannot represent its negation. For a fixed question and component, each candidate with a scoreable logit gets the competition rank $\mathrm{rank}_i = 1 + |\{c' : s_i(c') > s_i(c)\}|$, so ranks are never compared across components and the uncalibrated logit scales stay harmless. A missing or unscorable logit receives the neutral midpoint $(n_i^{\mathrm{scoreable}}+1)/2$: a fixed, unoptimised convention under which \emph{missing is not false}, but an evidence-free candidate can outrank a weakly evidenced one. With $\mathrm{RR}_i = 1/\mathrm{rank}_i$ over the $m^{+}$ positive components,
\begin{equation*}
S_{\mathrm{req}} = \exp\!\left(\tfrac{1}{m^{+}}\textstyle\sum_i \log(\mathrm{RR}_i + \varepsilon)\right), \qquad S_{\mathrm{weak}} = \min_i \mathrm{RR}_i, \qquad \varepsilon = 10^{-12}.
\end{equation*}
Four tiers are assigned: tier 3 if any component is \texttt{CONTRADICTED} after exclusion polarity; tier 0 if no contradiction and all positive components \texttt{SUPPORTED}; tier 1 if no contradiction and at least one \texttt{SUPPORTED} \emph{positive} component (positive-only by definition, corrected before the freeze on semantic and reviewer grounds, never from gold); tier 2 otherwise. The final order is lexicographic: tier ascending, $S_{\mathrm{req}}$ descending, $S_{\mathrm{weak}}$ descending, global relevance competition rank ascending, fusion position ascending, entity identifier. No weight, threshold or pool size is learned or fitted.

