\section*{Method}

\paragraph{Data and identity.} The original question string is always preserved and is always what the global relevance model sees. Visibility is publication-year only (\texttt{first\_seen\_year} at most the 2026 cutoff, with edge and asserting-article checks; \texttt{last\_seen\_year} is not an expiry; month constraints are unresolvable at year granularity). Identity grouping is exact surface equality after NFKC, casefold, whitespace and typographic-hyphen normalisation, only within compatible types, with the lowest member node identifier as canonical. Only graph aliases are used; no fuzzy inference and no target-derived correction. The 2026 index holds 2978 entities, 4274 evidence items, 10241 entity-evidence links, 6368 role arcs and 0 rejected edges, and 2508 entities have no candidate-specific evidence.

\paragraph{Candidate generation.} Hard answer-family filtering by question intent applies to all entity channels. Five families yield six lists, each capped at 500: dense original view; dense structured view; BM25 ($k_1=1.5$, $b=0.75$) over names, aliases and indexed evidence with positive overlaps only; conservative exact bounded names (digits, CamelCase, all-caps, or multiword of length at least 10); evidence-owner retrieval from 500 evidence seeds; and a bounded graph channel from the top 200 evidence seeds, at most two hops always through an article, article degree cap 80, fanout cap 64, decay $0.8^{\ell-1}$. Lists are fused over canonical identifiers by reciprocal rank fusion with $k=60$. Arms: A0 raw dense; A1 typed dense; A2 round-robin dense/BM25/name; A3 adds evidence; A4 adds graph; A5 full union by fusion; A6 relevance re-scoring of the 500-prefix; A7 conjunction ranking of the same prefix, predeclared primary and never selected from results. Controls: TypedRaw, ParsedOnly, WithoutEvidenceRRF, WithoutGraphRRF, relevance depth 100/200/500, A7\_NoNLI (all NLI ignored, every candidate forced to tier 2, reusing the same component relevance scores) and A7\_SingleEvidence (evidence $k=1$, both models run independently).

\paragraph{Evidence and models.} For each prefix candidate and component, only legitimately attached candidate-specific evidence is ranked, by similarity, then relation priority (direct claim, explicit mention, typed evidence), then evidence identifier; article and graph-evidence fields are excluded; normalised duplicates are removed; the top $k=3$ blocks are kept. Packing is identity-first within 512 tokens, keeps whole evidence blocks while they fit, and records inclusions, omissions and query truncation; a bundle with no packed evidence gets a null component logit. Pinned models, exact revisions from \path{config.json}: dense \texttt{BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5} (\texttt{5c38ec7c405ec4b44b94}\allowbreak\texttt{cc5a9bb96e735b38267a}); genuine relevance \texttt{cross-encoder/ms-marco-MiniLM-L6-v2} (\texttt{233902d25c440f23af6f}\allowbreak\texttt{7d6e94d2946bac0bee0a}) for the global question score and for per-component scores; support proxy \texttt{cross-encoder/nli-deberta-v3-small} (\texttt{fa2804872c3b4bd748f3}\allowbreak\texttt{8c0185cc85775361e735}). Roles are never interchanged: MiniLM measures relevance, DeBERTa measures entailment. One NLI pair per eligible packed bundle, premise = identity plus up to three evidence blocks packed jointly, hypothesis = the literal component statement; the exclusion template asserts a violation, so entailment and contradiction are swapped for the desired-status reading. Thresholds 0.7 with the opposing probability below 0.3; otherwise \texttt{NOT\_SUPPORTED\_BY\_AVAILABLE\_EVIDENCE}, or \texttt{NOT\_EVALUABLE} when evidence exists but NLI is unavailable. All logits and probabilities are uncalibrated.

\paragraph{Freeze and why the evaluation is trustworthy as far as it goes.} \path{predict.py} and \path{evaluate.py} are separate processes. The predictor reads only graph, questions, config, its own source and the pinned models, imports nothing from the evaluator, and runs under a strict input allowlist that blocks old outputs, archives, reports, notes, gold, mappings and oracles; every project-relative read is logged and a freeze is impossible while any denied read exists. The frozen run records 4186 project reads with \textbf{0 denied reads, 0 gold reads, 0 historical evaluation reads}. Model files are hashed before loading and revisions must match config. Prediction hashes config, source, inputs, model manifest and generated artefacts, then freezes; the digest is \texttt{2d7485f1d0ecfb541d1d83413e2ac1d9}\allowbreak\texttt{61519ce9c1e0870dbd74311462918570}. The evaluator verifies every hash before importing or reading gold and again afterwards, under a guard refusing any write, removal, rename or permission change on frozen files and all non-V2 writes. Gold mapping and positive controls are evaluation-only. Weights are frozen: no optimiser, fine-tuning, training, benchmark fit or grid search; the benchmark did not select the pool size 500 or the evidence $k=3$. Seed 42, CPU 4 threads, batch 32 for dense and component relevance, 16 for global relevance and NLI. Caches are content-addressed and previously evaluated predictions are never reused; a cached replay verifies byte identity and is \emph{not} an independent uncached inference run. Determinism tests cover the dense and global relevance paths; NLI determinism is not covered, so NLI test coverage is limited. Enforcement is an allowlist plus a cooperative Python audit hook, not an operating-system sandbox. \textbf{Validity limit: all results are development results. The freeze prevents run-time gold access, not design-time exposure.}

